## Description of work
The grouping-schema map provides a centralized resource, allowing the CIS to specify which grouping files are applicable to instrument states in each of the `lite` or `native` instrument modes.  Using the `FocusGroup` class, this map also allows the association of a simple _name_ to each of these grouping files.  A default version of this grouping-schema map is placed at the `<instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home>` location.  At initialization of a new `InstrumentState` version tree, a copy of this file is written to the `<state root>` directory.

## Explanation of work
Grouping-schema map, DAO implementation:
  The changes of this commit include:
  * Implementation of class `GroupingMap`, providing access to maps of `FocusGroup` applicable to a given `InstrumentState`;
  * Separate `FocusGroup` maps are provided for each of `native` and `lite` modes;
  * The associated JSON representation of the `GroupingMap` uses separate _lists_ to provide an easy to edit format for by-hand editing (by the CIS);
  * During its intialization process, only _valid_ `FocusGroup` are added to a `GroupingMap` instance;
  * Valid `FocusGroup` paths must exist, and must have a valid file format;
  * Invalid `FocusGroup` found during initialization are _logged_ as `warning`, but initialization is allowed to continue;
  * A relative path in a `FocusGroup` is referenced with respect to <instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home> from `Config`;
  * An absolute path in a `FocusGroup` is allowed, and will accepted without modification, provided that the path is a valid `FocusGroup` path;

Grouping-schema map, connection to `InstrumentState` and `LocalDataService`:

  * `GroupingMap` has a `stateId` attribute, allowing association to only one <instrument.state.root> (which actually, may be the parent of several _versions_ of the state);
  * The <default grouping map> at <instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home> has a special <default grouping-map state id>;
  * A new `ObjectSHA` class enforces required behavior of the <state id>, including: -- a standard hex-digest format: 16-character, lowercase hex string; -- initialization, or read and write of the state-id from a simple string; -- optional (though non-persistent) retention of the sometimes-provided `decodedKey` field (used nowhere at present);
  * `GroupingMap` is added as an attribute to `InstrumentState`: -- implementation of an _explicit_ method `attachGroupingMap` with optional coercion of the `GroupingMap.stateId` to match that of the `InstrumentState`; -- use of a _root_validator_ to enforce that `InstrumentState.groupingMap.stateId` == `InstrumentState`.id;
  * A state's `GroupingMap` has a separate JSON file to that of the `InstrumentState`: -- appropriate methods were added to `LocalDataService` to implement this file-separation behavior: note that this includes calling `InstrumentState.attachGroupingMap` in many existing _read_ methods; -- required modifications to existing tests in `LocalDataService`; -- the names of several tests were updated to include the behavior of what the tests are actually testing; hopefully this will help _future_ maintainers;
  * During the initialization of an `InstrumentState`: -- read of the <default grouping map> from the correct location at <instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home>; -- write of the grouping map to the correct location at <state root> (i.e. at the _root_ of the state's version tree); -- `GroupingMap` write only occurs only _once_ at initializion of a _new_ state version tree (and _overwrite_ is not allowed);


## To test

### Dev testing
Unit tests were added at `test_GroupingMap.py` and at `test_LocalDataService.py`.  The former test the basic `GroupingMap` implementation, and in combination with the latter, all of the key _behavior_ requirements of the story are verified.


### CIS testing
  * A copy of `defaultGroupingMap.json` should be placed at <instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home> on the SNS filesystem (the filename must not be modified);
  * Any applicable grouping-file paths should then be added to the JSON lists contained in this file; for grouping files residing in <instrument.calibration.powder.grouping.home> these files can be added as simple filenames; note that the `stateId` field should _not_ be modified; this field has a special value reserved for this _default_ version of the grouping-schema map;
  * Using the SNAPRed GUI, any operation that _initializes_ an `InstrumentState` should be performed;

  Following a new state initialization: a new `groupingMap.json` should have been placed at the _root_ of the state version tree.  The contents of this JSON should match that of the `defaultGroupingMap.json`, except for the `stateId` field, which should have been updated to match that of the new state.

